- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** AT-2 starts its kit (001 §1b; 001 §Q 'Common rules' 'Build: each test builds its kit ONLY through the semantic messages (§P), against a SQLite `:memory:` library, and writes it through the REAL folder `KitProxy` into a throw-away folder under the test run's output directory'; 001 §Q AT-2 'Kit: a source at `referenceWaveLength`; an ideal polarimeter detector with the `NoiseParam.decentLab` noise model; five sample items — 100 µm plates cut … — all made of ONE material version holding the `absorbing` ground truth'). A crystal material reaches the library through its entry file (step 355), so the build drops the material and its plate sample on the Library window, as a user drops files they were given (001 §H; steps 104, 111). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs` (step 421), each private function documented in one line citing spec 0050 S12.2: (1) Shared with AT-1, so one composition exists (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'): the test clock and the start screen `buildOpticsMuellerKit` composes inline (step 421 (c), (d)) become `testClockAt (instant : ClockTime)`, answering a `ClockProvider` over a mutable cell and that cell, which only a build sets to move its clock, and `kitStartOver (context : AppContext) (clock : ClockProvider) (kitId : KitId) (author : KitAuthor) (folder : KitFolder)`, the `KitStartModel` and the cell its `showKit` keeps the opened kit in; `buildOpticsMuellerKit` calls them with its own values, and every AT-1 fact keeps its assertions. (2) `buildAbsorbingKit (run : FolderName)`, which later steps extend, answers the built folder, the app context, the window model and the test clock, in this order. (a) The folder is `<System.AppContext.BaseDirectory>/KitAcceptanceTests/<run>/absorbing-biaxial-noisy`, created fresh and empty, its leaf naming the kit (step 145). (b) The context is `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitAcceptanceTests")` (steps 83, 100). (c) The clock is `testClockAt` 2026-06-01T12:00:00Z (UTC), advanced only by the build. (d) The two entry files, written outside the kit under `<System.AppContext.BaseDirectory>/KitAcceptanceTests/<run>/entries/`: each `LibraryEntryContent` (step 25) at the first version under `UserProvenance` (step 24), `sealed` then `fileText` (step 30), written as that text, UTF-8 without a byte-order mark, under its `fileName`. The material: `ofMaterialEntry` of the entry `MaterialId (Guid.Parse "81e1d115-5d06-4337-80fd-50765a403de7")`, `EntryName "Absorbing triclinic crystal"`, category `CategoryIds.crystal`, the description `The fifteen-parameter absorbing, gyrotropic, triclinic crystal of spec 0044 (AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbing).` and the physics `CrystalParameterPhysics (AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbing)` (steps 354, 355; `BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:absorbing`), every other field as `MaterialProxyTests` mints its absorbing crystal material (step 355). The sample: `ofSample` of `SampleId (Guid.Parse "af711361-2854-4b61-ade4-bdb47a184d9f")`, `EntryName "Absorbing triclinic plate 100 um"`, the structure `{ films = []; substrate = Some { materialId = MaterialVersionId.firstOf <the material's id>; thickness = AbsorbingBiaxialSample.plate; orientation = PrimaryAxes }; lower = None }` (`ElementId.fs:SampleStructure`), `ThickPlate`, the description `A 100 um plate of the absorbing triclinic crystal; each observation carries its cut.` and `EmitBoth`. (e) The drop: a Library window model (`initLibraryWindow` in Browse mode, step 111) over the context's stores and import seam, as `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` builds one, whose `openImportDialog` keeps the request it is given; `DropLibraryEntryFiles [ <the material file>; <the sample file> ]` opens it over `ApplyDroppedEntries` of two rows whose default action adds the entry (steps 93, 104); an import dialog model (`initImportDialog`, step 107) over `context.catalogueImports`, that request, an `onApplied` that keeps the `ImportDialogApplied` and a `requestClose` that does nothing takes `ApplyImportChoices`, and the Library window takes `LibraryImportApplied` of what was kept. The material and the sample are then in the SQLite library at version 1. (f) The kit: `kitStartOver context clock (KitId (Guid.Parse "e15b30f6-b9ff-4a6b-a88d-b5401df2a7ae")) (KitAuthor "absorbing-biaxial-noisy bench") <the folder>` and `CreateKit` of the folder (steps 177, 420). The window model is `TestAppScope.inverseModelOver context <the opened kit>` (step 421), whose `itemIds` is replaced by a test-local `ItemIdProvider` answering, call by call, Laser `9f304813-02a2-4624-b7e3-eea3e75193e7`, Polarimeter T `f7e47d80-d265-481e-b351-6e6bf48785ee`, Polarimeter R `938e1eb1-4b3d-43ea-b4a0-12c1dc5c4191`, OpticAxisCut `f61f5339-1db2-4c6c-a453-a9a9f0c11594`, OtherOpticAxisCut `10409181-5b7a-47b6-82df-525608098a65`, ZCut `1a62e3fd-a168-4c03-a653-1ed3ae71789b`, XCut `d64587f5-a4dd-4d6e-b85d-c6fecdc24f9b`, YCut `5b34e704-1b59-4aa7-9904-f5ccbbb3ef71`. (g) The naming template: `SetNamingTemplateText (ControlCaption "{obj1}")` and `SaveNamingTemplate` (step 273), so setups and experiments are named by the plate in Object 1 (steps 271, 286). (h) The eight items, each through `OpenAddItemForm`, `ChooseNewItemModel` of the form's offer, `SetNewItemLabel` and `AddItem` of the form's draft (step 239), every one `FixedMounting`, in this order: `Laser`, the `PresetIds.heNe633` source preset, whose 632.8 nm is `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.waveLength` (`referenceWaveLength`); `Polarimeter T` and `Polarimeter R`, the Mueller polarimeter (`ItemModelIds.muellerPolarimeterModelId`), whose noise axes default to `NoiseParam.decentLab`'s budget (steps 207, 208, 210); and the five plates `OpticAxisCut`, `OtherOpticAxisCut`, `ZCut`, `XCut` and `YCut`, each the form's `StackSampleChoice` of the dropped sample (step 239). No parameter state is set: every parameter stays known at its default. (i) The table: `AssignSlot` (step 263) puts `Laser` in `src`, `OpticAxisCut` in `sample` and `Polarimeter T` in `det` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:initInverse`); then `AddElement Detector` adds a detector, `PlaceOnBeam (<that element's id>, BeamLayout.OnReflectedBeamOf (Library.ElementId "sample"))` puts it on the plate's reflected ray, and `AssignSlot` puts `Polarimeter R` in it, so the plate is captured in transmission and reflection (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:availableCaptures`). (3) `absorbingBuild`, a module-level `Lazy` of `buildAbsorbingKit (FolderName "AT-2")`, documented in one line: every AT-2 fact but the ensemble (step 437) reads this one build, so the build and the fit it ends with (step 436) run once per test run; xUnit runs one class's facts one at a time, and no fact writes into the built folder or changes the shared model, a fact that sends a message folding it over its own copy. Each AT-2 fact asserts what its part of the build writes, which the later parts keep. (4) The fact `AT-2 builds the absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit's library entries, items and table through the app's messages`: after the build, a second `KitProxy.create` of the built folder reads `.kit-json` holding the id above, the name `absorbing-biaxial-noisy`, the author `absorbing-biaxial-noisy bench`, created and modified at 2026-06-01T12:00:00Z, the template `{obj1}`, no import profile and no send exclusion; `readItems` the eight items with the ids, labels and models above, `FixedMounting`, revision 1 and every parameter `KnownParameter` at its default, the two polarimeters' `rotationUncertainty`, `elementUncertainty` and `throughputUncertainty` equal to `NoiseParam.decentLab.parameterAxes`' defaults and each plate's `substrate.thickness` equal to `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.plate` in metres (step 207); and `library/` holds exactly four snapshots, the material and the sample each byte-identical to its dropped file and the `heNe633` preset and the Mueller polarimeter model each byte-identical to its `Catalogue/Builtin/` file. Each assertion's message names the file and both values. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. KitAcceptanceTests.fs MUST open OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise for NoiseParam and its parameterAxes member; Domain holds only the detector axis descriptors.

**Acceptance.** After AT-2's first part lands, `KitAcceptanceTests` MUST build the absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit through the Library window's drop, the import dialog, the start screen and the kit window's messages alone: one material and one sample in the SQLite library, the kit file, eight items and a table capturing the plate in T and R, and AT-1 MUST compose its clock and start screen through the same two functions; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-2 builds the absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit's library entries, items and table through the app's messages`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s42 invariants MUST pass.
